// spec: required `override` (design.md 23b): a function that overrides a virtual one says so, `override` or `final`, an error at its declaration, in a class and per instance of a class template whose base is its parameter (naming the instance), as is an instance's `override` of nothing (a mixin over a plain base); a destructor, `final`, a hiding non-virtual, a new function and an out-of-line definition, which cannot say it, are not
